body:
@mfreed7 thanks for thinking all this through & providing feedback. I know it's frustrating opening this stuff up after it feels like the work was 'done', so I really appreciate it.

> One issue is that while we can throw for `auto.showPopover({source: hint})`, we can't do that for a declarative invocation (via `commandfor` or `popovertarget`). But we can just make that _not_ open the target popover, and a console warning should do the job of notifying the author.

Yeah, I agree with all that. It'll also happen for things that use popovers under the hood, like custom `<select>`.
